// TEST: An anonymous index cast of an out-of-range literal is refused (rejects)
// ============================================================================
// Gap G208 (3), round 4 wave 8 (lane C, C5): an ANONYMOUS index ascription
// `(e : Idx<3>)` is the same cast into an index space as a named one: a
// literal is range-checked at compile time (BL4003) and a computed integer
// gets the checked conversion (BL8006 at run time, every lane). It used to
// make `(5 : Idx<3>)` an unchecked position (an anonymous tag is never proof;
// only reads THROUGH it were checked).
// ============================================================================
let i = (5 : Idx<3>)
// ERROR: BL4003
// ERROR-CONTAINS: the literal position 5 is out of range for Idx<3>
// REJECT-AT: lower
